  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A body when fully immersed in a liquid of specific gravity 1.2 weighs 44 gwt. The same body when fully immersed in water weighs 50 gwt. The mass of the body is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wNQpO",
      "text": "36 \\mathrm{g}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4jw6F",
      "text": "48 \\mathrm{g}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "KF8XM",
      "text": "64 \\mathrm{g}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "mhXjE",
      "text": "$80 \\mathrm{g}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Balancing equation\r\n$$\r\nW=m g-V \\rho g\r\n$$\r\nHence,\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{l}\r\n44=m-1.2 \\mathrm{V} \\\\\r\n50=m-V\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$\r\nOn solving Eqs. (i) and (ii) we get\r\n$$\r\nm=80 \\mathrm{g}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
